        "items": [
          "Simple, independent values",
          "A few setters"
        ]
      },
      "right": {
        "title": "useReducer",
        "color": "green",
        "items": [
          "Related state together",
          "Many ways to update it"
        ]
      },
      "say": "Use State is perfect for simple values. When several pieces of state change together, or there are many different ways to update them, use Reducer keeps all that logic in one place.",
      "voice": "/audio/react-10-usereducer/when.wav"
    },
    {
      "id": "reducer",
      "min": 9,
      "duration": 11.0,
      "text": "A reducer is a pure function.",
      "visual": "code",
      "items": [
        [
          "function reducer(state, action) {",
          "yellow"
        ],
        [
          "  switch (action.type) {",
          "blue"
        ],
        [
          "    case 'add':",
          "green"
        ],
        [
          "      return [...state, action.todo];",
          "green"
        ],
        [
          "    case 'remove':",
          "green"
        ],
        [
          "      return state.filter(t =>",
          "green"
        ],
        [
          "        t.id !== action.id);",
          "green"
        ],
        [
          "  }",
          "blue"
        ],
        [
          "}",
          "yellow"
        ]
      ],
      "say": "A reducer takes the current state and an action, and returns the next state. It is a pure function, with a switch on the action type, and it never mutates the state it was given.",
      "voice": "/audio/react-10-usereducer/reducer.wav"
    },
    {
      "id": "use",
      "min": 8,
      "duration": 9.5,
      "text": "Dispatch actions.",
      "visual": "code",
      "items": [
        [
          "const [todos, dispatch] =",
          "yellow"
        ],
        [
          "  useReducer(reducer, []);",
          "yellow"
        ],
        [
          "",
          "text"
        ],
        [
          "dispatch({ type: 'add', todo });",
          "green"
        ],
        [
          "dispatch({ type: 'remove', id });",
          "green"
        ]
      ],
      "say": "The hook gives you the state, and a dispatch function. Instead of calling setters, components dispatch small action objects that describe what happened.",
      "voice": "/audio/react-10-usereducer/use.wav"
    },
    {
      "id": "flow",
      "min": 8,
      "duration": 11.5,
      "text": "The reducer loop.",
      "visual": "flow",
      "badge": "EVENTS DESCRIBED, NOT PERFORMED",
      "items": [
        [
          "dispatch(action)",
          "yellow",
          "describes what happened"
        ],
        [
          "reducer(state, action)",
          "blue",
          "a pure function"
        ],
        [
          "New state",
          "green",
          "the component re-renders"
        ]
      ],
      "say": "The flow is simple. An event dispatches an action. React calls your reducer with the old state and that action. The returned value becomes the new state, and the component re-renders.",
      "voice": "/audio/react-10-usereducer/flow.wav"
    },
    {
      "id": "benefits",
      "min": 8,
      "duration": 11.5,
      "text": "Why teams like reducers.",
      "visual": "chips",
      "items": [
        [
          "All update logic in one place",
          "green"
        ],
        [
          "Easy to test: just a function",
